SVsXy9", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 375534, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Q1AWmdR99A2JQZR1SVsXy9", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 379565, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` says it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but the code used ROUND_HALF_UP. So `2.665` became `2.67` when the test expects `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed one line so it uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101 is at https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101.\n\nWhen I tried to look up FIN-212, the advisory system didn't recognize it. It's probably an internal finance reference rather than a security advisory, so I relied on the test and the code comment.\n\nI haven't merged the PR. Policy says merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SGU1hdRYZEfdvDEXktnY9m", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017oHrtsxspXYs38z9ZVtqPE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01HxJ7ZuhZijin8FVaRAeve3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id":